From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:43:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s800-0-3: Turn the display pipe on for
 every A9 board

The IPSW device trees of all ten A9 boards describe the same display
pipe and display DART (ADT disp0 "adbe0,s8000" and dart-disp0, equal
but for phandles), so the pipe moves from s8003.dtsi to the shared A9
file, on by default, and the Samsung iPads and the iPhones get it too.
The DART stays off until the driver turns translated scanout on, as
before.

What differs is the panel link, and the board files say it: the iPad 5
drives eDP (ADT displayport), so its pipe holds the dp domain and has
the DisplayPort transmitter's window and the panel supply, now on all
four iPad 5 models without the S800X_IPAD5_DISPLAY_PIPE define. The
iPhones drive MIPI DSI (ADT mipi-dsim) and hold the mipi_dsi domain.
Where the driver doesn't find the pipe as iBoot left it, the boot
framebuffer keeps the display.

Assisted-by: LLM
